Approach (Floyd’s Cycle Detection)
Treat the array as a linked list where:
Index represents the current node
Value at index represents the next node
Since one number is duplicated, it creates a cycle in this structure.
Use two pointers:
slow moves one step at a time
fast moves two steps at a time
First, detect the meeting point inside the cycle.
Then reset slow to the start and move both pointers one step at a time.
The point where they meet again is the duplicate number (cycle entry).
Complexity
Time Complexity: O(n)
Space Complexity: O(1)
